# Cloudflare Pages redirects/rewrites.
#
# Clean URLs (/streets -> /streets.html etc.) are handled AUTOMATICALLY by Pages,
# so the per-page .html rewrites from vercel.json are not needed here.
#
# The SPA-style catch-all (`/*  /index.html  200`) that preserved Vercel's old
# behaviour was REMOVED 2026-08-13. It made every unknown path a soft-404: the
# homepage returned with HTTP 200, which search engines treat as duplicate
# content, and which meant deleted endpoints (the legacy /api/*.js handlers)
# answered 200 instead of 404 after their files were removed. Every real route
# on this site is a real file — Pages resolves clean URLs itself — so the
# catch-all only ever matched genuine 404s.
#
# Unknown paths now fall through to /404.html (src/404.njk), which Pages serves
# automatically with a real 404 status.
